    deepExplanation: "Example:\n\n```ts\n// Secure-by-default API wrapper: never interpolate secrets into URLs.\nexport async function getJson<T>(url: string): Promise<T> {\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n    credentials: \"same-origin\",\n    headers: { Accept: \"application/json\" },\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n  return response.json() as Promise<T>;\n}\n```\n\nProduction pattern:\n\n```ts\n// Validate security-sensitive state at the boundary.\nfunction isAllowedOrigin(origin: string, allowed: readonly string[]) {\n  return allowed.includes(origin);\n}\n\nconsole.log(isAllowedOrigin(\"https://app.example.com\", [\n  \"https://app.example.com\",\n]));\n```\n\nWhy it matters: Prevents account compromise, data exposure and unauthorized actions. Reduces exploitable browser and supply-chain attack surface. Makes security controls reviewable, testable and observable.",
